<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<databaseChangeLog
        xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
        xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
            http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-latest.xsd">

    <!--
      Wave 03 "PRIME": the second widget returns to the board: the latest drop (DESIGN §10.2),
      in the "frame" edition (`edition: "frame"`): one random photo filling the card, the caption
      in the bottom band of the progressive blur.

      The composition turns from a column into a pair. The "music over the switcher" column stood
      on the axis of column 20; the drop is a tile of the same weight as music, and putting it above or
      below would stretch the column to three quarters of the screen's height. Instead the drop
      stands to the LEFT of the column. The GROUP must centre on the grid: 10 + spacer + 10 = 21
      columns on the even 40 grid misses the axis by half a column: the same 19px that
      the 0530 seed caught for the lone column. So the drop is one column wider than music (11):
      the group is 11 + 1 + 10 = 22 columns, columns 10–31, nine empty on each side.
      For this the column moves right by six columns (16→22, 18→24); within the pair the
      "music over the switcher" axis is kept.

      The rows are a SLOT, not a tile. The frame card takes the photo's own proportion (the owner's
      decision): a landscape frame is a landscape card across the slot's width, a portrait one a portrait card across
      the slot's height, both centred in the slot. So the slot is reserved as a SQUARE with
      a margin, so that no orientation runs into the neighbours: 11 columns ≈ 413px, 16 rows ≈
      448px at the 1536 reference: a square within 8%. Rows 6–21: the slot's centre is row 14, the same
      as the column on the right (music 8–14 + switcher 16–19), i.e. the pair sits on
      one horizontal axis, and the optical centre is still above the geometric one.

      Mobile order: the drop between music and the switcher: the switcher stays
      last, as on every wave (a control closes the stack rather than opening it).
    -->
    <changeSet id="0590-wave-03-latest-drop" author="danchuo">
        <sql><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(
                jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,latestDrop}', $J${"col": 10, "row": 6, "colSpan": 11, "rowSpan": 16, "edition": "frame"}$J$::jsonb),
                '{tiles,music}',
                $J${"col": 22, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 7}$J$::jsonb
            ),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 24, "row": 16, "colSpan": 6, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["music", "latestDrop", "waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></sql>
        <rollback><![CDATA[
UPDATE theme
SET layout = jsonb_set(
        jsonb_set(
            jsonb_set(
                jsonb_set(layout, '{tiles,latestDrop}', $J${"hidden": true}$J$::jsonb),
                '{tiles,music}',
                $J${"col": 16, "row": 8, "colSpan": 10, "rowSpan": 7}$J$::jsonb
            ),
            '{tiles,waveSwitcher}',
            $J${"col": 18, "row": 16, "colSpan": 6, "rowSpan": 4}$J$::jsonb
        ),
        '{mobileOrder}',
        $J$["music", "waveSwitcher"]$J$::jsonb
    )
WHERE key = 'wave-03';
        ]]></rollback>
    </changeSet>
</databaseChangeLog>
